    {
      "text": "If it senses strong sunlight, it opens its folded petals to absorb the sun’s rays with its whole body.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "As a bud, it barely moves. It sits still, placidly waiting for sunlight to appear.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its folded petals are pretty tough. Bird Pokémon can peck at them all they want, and Cherrim won’t be bothered at all.",
      "version": "shield"
    },
    {
      "text": "Motionless, save for the occasional quiver. A rich array of Pokémon can be found gathered around it, drawn by the scent exuded from Cherrim's folded petals.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
